
  iMac Display installer  (Arch Linux + Claude Code)

  This stick installs Linux on the iMac's internal drive, next to macOS.

  First, in macOS on the iMac:
    1. Make a Time Machine backup.
    2. Disk Utility > View > Show All Devices > select the internal drive >
       Partition > "+" > Add Partition. Make two, format "MS-DOS (FAT)":
           LINUXBOOT    1 GB
           LINUX        60 GB or more (20 GB minimum)

  Then here, type:

       imac-install

  It erases only the partitions named LINUXBOOT and LINUX, and asks first.
  No internet is needed.

  Also on this stick:  m0-check (hardware facts)   iwctl (Wi-Fi)   claude

